{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795543748,"nonce":"3SEGZ4yoq57el3HkUGe98vZ8lgs=","target":"f501dde0361fe6a22ac9cda0711a289a8f278fc02b44ebee0a99819c6a375f06","message":"`value_and_grad` of a loss through `jno.litho.CAResist` is about three times slower at 07593516 (0.4.3) than at ca0181ee, with the litho module unchanged between them. The case is the 2-D bake rebuilt by `jno.fem` on every call: 3 coupled fields, 30 backward-Euler steps with Newton.\n\n**Measurement.** Warm median of 5 `value_and_grad` calls, each version in its own process, same image and settings. The cached-bake `CAResist` on branch perf/caresist-build-once avoids the rebuild and no longer shows it, but any caller that builds a `jno.fem` per call pays the cost.\n\n**Bisect.** The slowdown comes from the squash merge of #170. Within it, the seeded test-function path (the element residual as the gradient of a seeded integrand, the tangent forward over reverse) added the most trace work. A seeded kernel traces slower on every element family tried, and a scalar test field gains no run time from it on CPU or GPU, while 3-D vector tangents do gain on the GPU.\n\n**Fix so far.** Commit 40a2075d (branch perf/caresist-build-once, not merged yet) seeds only test fields with several components. For the scalar rebuild case, primitive binds per warm call drop from 41.5k to 34.1k (28.3k before #170; profile of one warm `value_and_grad` through a per-call-rebuilt 2-D `CAResist` bake). Test, on the same branch: `tests/test_fem_seeded_test_function.py::test_by_default_only_a_test_field_with_several_components_is_seeded`.\n\n**Direction.** The remaining growth comes from other #170 changes, spread over tracing the inexact-Newton Krylov path in the step, `_symmetrise_own_block` on every tangent and the block-compressed scatter plan, with no single dominant function. Next step is a per-function primitive-bind count across the 28.3k to 34.1k gap, then decide which of the three to trim or cache across rebuilds.","files":null}]}